== Delta ==
getpid  1050.7 -> 934.8 ns  (-116 ns, -11%)  [poll() itimer-scan+closure removed]
pipe_wr 5913.9 -> 5844.1 ns (-70 ns, 2 syscalls)
Accuracy: EXACT — rusage_acct identical to OFF and matches Linux (s_frac 0.72, cpu/wall 1.00, verdict PASS).

## SMP-safe re-run (2026-08-09, after thr.time RefCell->SpinNoIrq, commit 710eed8c3)
# Both configs boot to shell + run to completion (no deadlock on real 8-core);
# rusage_acct exercises getrusage (now a lock) repeatedly; both PASS.
== StarryOS OFF (placement, SMP-safe) ==
SYSCOST getpid  1026.5 ns/syscall
SYSCOST pipe_wr  6231.0 ns
RUSAGE_ACCT user    cpu/wall=1.00 u_frac=1.00  PASS
RUSAGE_ACCT syscall cpu/wall=1.00 s_frac=0.68  PASS
== StarryOS ON (tickacct, SMP-safe) ==
SYSCOST getpid  1031.0 ns/syscall
SYSCOST pipe_wr  6133.7 ns
RUSAGE_ACCT user    cpu/wall=1.00 u_frac=1.00  PASS
RUSAGE_ACCT syscall cpu/wall=1.00 s_frac=0.68  PASS
## Finding: tickacct's pre-SMP -116ns getpid win was the per-boundary emitter
## CLOSURE construction in the old poll(emitter). The SMP-safe poll() returns
## signals (no closure) -> the OFF path gained that win too, so ON~=OFF now.
## SMP-safe SpinNoIrq lock costs ~96ns/syscall (ON 935->1031). Net: tickacct is
## now perf-NEUTRAL; its value is correct uniform all-CPU accounting. Accounting
## stays exact (rusage_acct PASS, s_frac 0.68 both, matches Linux ~0.72 band).
